  <section class="section mist">
    <div class="wrap faq">
      <h2>About the service</h2>
      <details><summary>What is dataleasers?</summary><p>We introduce operating companies to Mode, which buys and licenses company data. We describe the programme and answer what we can; we do not advise on the agreements or your data rights, and your own counsel can review those.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What is Mode?</summary><p>Mode is the team that takes data licensing for AI forward once an introduction is made. They assess the opportunity and lead discussions with buyers.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do I have to sell my data?</summary><p>No. A first call carries no commitment. Nothing moves forward without your approval.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Who are the buyers?</summary><p>AI teams that need real business records to train and test models. See <a href="who-buys.html">Who buys</a>.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What kinds of data do you work with?</summary><p>Conversations, customer support, documents, code and engineering, sales records and operations. See <a href="what-you-can-sell.html">What you can sell</a>.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section teal-soft">
    <div class="wrap faq">
      <h2>Rights and personal data</h2>
      <details><summary>Can I sell data my customers created?</summary><p>It depends on your contracts and the tool's terms. Mode reviews this before any buyer sees the data.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Is anonymised data safe to share?</summary><p>Removing names does not make data anonymous. Mode gives personal information its own review.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What if we cannot license everything?</summary><p>Mode will tell you before anything moves, and the scope can often be narrowed to what is clear.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do you handle health or financial data?</summary><p>Some of it is subject to strict rules. Mode reviews these case by case and may decline.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can a buyer use the data however they like?</summary><p>No. Scope, purpose and length of licence are set in the terms you approve. See <a href="what-affects-a-deal.html">What affects a deal</a>.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section mist">
    <div class="wrap faq">
      <h2>Money and terms</h2>
      <details><summary>How much could my data be worth?</summary><p>We do not publish prices, because value depends on the data, the rights and the terms. We discuss it on a call.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What fees apply?</summary><p>Mode buys the copy directly and charges no broker fee. The price and payment schedule are set in the agreement you sign.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Are there referral fees?</summary><p>Yes. Mode pays $50,000 or 6% of the partnership value, whichever is bigger, if a company you introduce becomes a qualified data partner and the deal closes. Payment is confirmed in writing. See <a href="refer.html">Refer a company</a>.</p></details>
      <details><summary>When do I get paid?</summary><p>Mode pays you directly, on the schedule set in your agreement, once it accepts the data.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section teal-soft">
    <div class="wrap faq">
      <h2>Working with us</h2>
      <details><summary>How long does it take?</summary><p>Mode generally expects about three months from the first conversation to payment. The steps depend on scope, rights review and export.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Is the first call confidential?</summary><p>Yes. We use the details you share only to reply to your enquiry. See <a href="trust.html">How we handle your data</a>.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I stop at any point?</summary><p>Yes. You approve every step, so you can decide not to continue.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>

